# Hodge Spectral Duality — Seventh Cycle

This file is the **synthesis** cycle of the discrete-Hodge program.  It welds the two
previously separate strands:

* the *decomposition / spectral foundation*
  `Catalog/Speculative/AutoResearch/HodgeSpectralThreshold.lean`
  (`hodgeLaplacian`, `harmonic_iff`, `ker_hodgeLaplacian`, `hodgeLaplacian_symm`), and
* the *spectral representation of message passing*
  `Catalog/Speculative/AutoResearch/HodgeMessagePassingDuality.lean`
  (`mpStep_eigen`, `mpStep_iterate_eigen`, `mpStep_eigen_energy`, `mpStep_symm`,
  `mpStep_fixed_iff`, `mpStep_eigenspace_one`),

into a single statement about the *full* Hodge Laplacian `Δ = up + down`.

The decisive new phenomenon is **eigenvalue additivity**: on a cochain that is a
*simultaneous* eigenvector of the up and down pieces (`up x = a•x`, `down x = b•x`),
the Hodge Laplacian acts as the scalar `a + b` (`hodgeLaplacian_joint_eigen`).  Feeding
this into the spectral representation of message passing shows that one layer
`T = 1 - α·Δ` acts as the scalar `1 - α(a+b)` (`mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen`), every depth
iterate as `(1 - α(a+b))ᵏ` (`mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen_iterate`), and the energy of such
a joint mode after `k` layers is *exactly* `(1 - α(a+b))^{2k}‖x‖²`
(`mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen_energy`).

Dually, at the *kernel* end of the spectrum the dynamical and algebraic descriptions
coincide on the nose: for a nonzero step the fixed points of full-Hodge message passing
are exactly the closed-and-coclosed (harmonic) cochains
(`mpStep_hodge_fixed_iff_harmonic`), and as submodules the unit eigenspace of message
passing equals the intersection of the two kernels
(`mpStep_hodge_eigenspace_one_eq_ker_inf`).  Finally the layer inherits the
self-adjointness of `Δ` (`mpStep_hodge_symm`).

The upshot: **the spectrum of full-Hodge message passing is the affine image
`1 - α·(spec(up) + spec(down))` on joint modes, and its fixed-point space is exactly
Hodge cohomology** — the two ends of the program, decomposition and dynamics, are one.

