Hypothesis:  The up/down split of the Hodge Laplacian should be *spectrally additive*:
  on a simultaneous eigenvector the eigenvalues add, so the whole message-passing
  representation theory of `HodgeMessagePassingDuality` (scalar action, exact energy,
  fixed ↔ kernel) lifts verbatim from a single operator `L` to the composite
  `Δ = up + down`, with eigenvalue `a + b`.  At the kernel end, `mpStep_fixed_iff`
  (`Tx = x ↔ Δx = 0`) composed with `harmonic_iff` (`Δx = 0 ↔ closed ∧ coclosed`) should
  identify fixed points with cohomology, and `mpStep_eigenspace_one` composed with
  `ker_hodgeLaplacian` should do the same at the submodule level.
Result:  Formalised and proved sorry-free.  `hodgeLaplacian_joint_eigen` (additive
  eigenvalues), `mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen` / `mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen_iterate`
  (scalar action of one / many layers), `mpStep_hodge_joint_eigen_energy` (exact
  `(1-α(a+b))^{2k}` energy), `mpStep_hodge_fixed_iff_harmonic` (fixed ↔ harmonic),
  `mpStep_hodge_eigenspace_one_eq_ker_inf` (unit eigenspace = `ker up ⊓ ker down`),
  and `mpStep_hodge_symm` (self-adjoint layer).
Insight:  Every theorem here is a *composition* of one decomposition fact with one
  dynamics fact — no new analysis is introduced.  The only genuinely new computation is
  `up x + down x = a•x + b•x = (a+b)•x` via `add_smul`; afterwards `mpStep_eigen`,
  `mpStep_fixed_iff`, `mpStep_eigenspace_one`, and `mpStep_symm` are instantiated at
  `L := hodgeLaplacian up down`, and the catalog's `harmonic_iff` / `ker_hodgeLaplacian`
  translate the kernel of `Δ` into the closed-and-coclosed data.
Failure analysis:  Stating eigenvalue additivity with `lam := a + b` (rather than
  carrying `a` and `b` separately through `mpStep_eigen`) keeps the energy and iterate
